{
  "name": "Probe-ListHandoff",
  "label": "Probe-ListHandoff: whether a list survives Run Shortcut, by crossing into itself (12 actions)",
  "actions": [
    {
      "id": "is.workflow.actions.comment",
      "p": {
        "WFCommentActionText": "Does a list survive Run Shortcut? Run-Pick's two-shortcut version passed [payload, verbs] across and the far side saw one newline-joined string, so the menu offered the payload as a choice. Whether that is true of every hand-off or only that one was never established, and it gates ever passing two arguments between shortcuts again. This settles it by crossing the boundary into ITSELF: bare, it builds a two-item list and re-enters; on the second pass it counts what arrived and logs it. count=2 first=AAA means lists survive. count=1 means they do not."
      }
    },
